      "content": "thanks, that's a really solid start. i like how you pointed out the \"short-term political gain\" part. i also want to make sure i address the opposition. if someone tries to argue that the city needs to prioritize things like fixing schools or roads instead of a stadium, how should i frame that argument so it sounds like a weak or poorly thought out excuse? like, how can i show that those \"budget concerns\" are just distractions from the real issue of growth?",
